# PowerShell and Python context

This Windows example writes JSON context in PowerShell and consumes it from an
isolated Python process.

```powershell {#powershell-setup independent=true}
Set-CtxValue greeting "hello from PowerShell"
Set-CtxValue samples @(3, 6, 9, 12)
Write-Output "PowerShell prepared $(Get-CtxValue greeting)"
```

```python {#python-consumer depends-on=powershell-setup}
ctx.total = sum(ctx.samples)
print(f"{ctx.greeting}: total={ctx.total}")
```

```python {#verify-powershell role=test test-of=python-consumer}
assert ctx.greeting == "hello from PowerShell"
assert ctx.total == 30
```
